---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import {
  AlertAccentDemo,
  AlertBannerDemo,
  AlertInlineDemo,
  AlertNeutralDemo,
} from "../../../components/react-demos/alert";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/react`;

const neutralHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="banner"
  data-tone="neutral"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">Mantenimiento programado</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      On Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC the panel will be read-only.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-alert__actions">
    <button
      class="sk-alert__dismiss"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Close alert"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>`;

const bannerHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="banner"
  data-tone="info"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="info"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">New version</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      An update is available.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>`;

const accentHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="accent"
  data-tone="warning"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="warning"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <p class="sk-alert__title">Your plan expires in 3 days</p>
    <div class="sk-alert__description">
      Choose a plan so as not to interrupt your deployments.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="sk-alert__actions">
    <a class="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/billing">View plans</a>
    <button
      class="sk-alert__dismiss"
      type="button"
      aria-label="Close alert"
    >
      <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>`;

const inlineHtml = `<div
  class="sk-alert"
  data-presentation="inline"
  data-tone="success"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
>
  <span class="sk-alert__icon" aria-hidden="true">
    <span data-sk-icon="success"></span>
  </span>
  <div class="sk-alert__content">
    <div class="sk-alert__description">Your changes have been saved.</div>
  </div>
</div>`;

const neutralReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

function SomeFunction() {}

function Example() {
  return (
    <Alert
      tone="neutral"
      title="Mantenimiento programado"
      onDismiss={SomeFunction}
    >
      On Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC the panel will be read-only.
    </Alert>
  );
}`;

const bannerReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

function Example() {
  return (
    <Alert tone="info" title="New version">
      An update is available.
    </Alert>
  );
}`;

const accentReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

function SomeFunction() {}

function Example() {
  return (
    <Alert
      onDismiss={SomeFunction}
      actions={
        <a className="sk-link sk-interactive" href="/billing">
          View plans
        </a>
      }
      presentation="accent"
      title="Your plan expires in 3 days"
      tone="warning"
    >
      Choose a plan so as not to interrupt your deployments.
    </Alert>
  );
}`;

const inlineReact = `import { Alert } from "@skryensya/react/alert";

function Example() {
  return (
    <Alert presentation="inline" tone="success">
      Your changes have been saved.
    </Alert>
  );
}`;
---

<Base title="Alert" description="Alert: Persistent inline message with tone (including neutral), accessible announcement and React component.">
  <h1>Alert</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Alert is an inline message that remains in the layout for the duration of its condition. Unlike Toast, which is transient and mounted in a floating region, Alert lives in the flow of content.
  </p>

  <h2>Tones</h2>
  <p>
    The tone decides whether the panel is painted with semantic color. <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code> and <code>danger</code> color the message. Only <code>danger</code> is advertised as <code>role="alert"</code> (assertive); the rest use <code>role="status"</code> (polite).
  </p>
  <p>
    All four read a <strong>feedback role</strong>, never the accent: the tone tells what happened, so it cannot change when the brand changes. <code>info</code> only had his own ramp in decision 26 (<code>docs/decisiones/0026-info-es-un-rol-de-feedback-no-el-acento.md</code>); Before, it read <code>accent</code>, and a magenta mark painted each information notice magenta.
  </p>

  <h3>Neutral</h3>
  <p>
    The default: surface and edge, without semantic painting. It exists for when the color should not be the prominent signal, the text (and, in a <a href="/en/components/toast">Toast</a>, the floating and disappearing) already loads the message. Use it in ordinary notices, short confirmations, or any case where painting the “success” or “info” panel would add urgency that the content does not have.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview html={neutralHtml} react={neutralReact} label="Alert neutral">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AlertNeutralDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h2>Presentations</h2>
  <p>Presentation decides visual weight, not urgency.</p>

  <h3>Banner</h3>
  <p>The full panel is for a condition that needs a title and explanation next to the affected content.</p>
  <ComponentPreview html={bannerHtml} react={bannerReact} label="Alert banner">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AlertBannerDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h3>Accent</h3>
  <p>The sidebar preserves the tone signal and lets a recovery action take center stage.</p>
  <ComponentPreview html={accentHtml} react={accentReact} label="Alert acento">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AlertAccentDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h3>Inline</h3>
  <p>Without panel or border, a short confirmation accompanies a block that already has its own structure.</p>
  <ComponentPreview html={inlineHtml} react={inlineReact} label="Alert inline">
    <Fragment slot="react">
      <AlertInlineDemo client:load />
    </Fragment>
  </ComponentPreview>

  <h2>Anatomy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>sk-alert__icon</code> is decorative and only appears when it provides a visual signal.</li>
    <li><code>sk-alert__content</code> groups optional title and description.</li>
    <li><code>sk-alert__actions</code> hosts actions that belong to the consumer; the optional closure lives there.</li>
    <li><code>data-tone</code> accepts <code>neutral</code> (default), <code>info</code>, <code>success</code>, <code>warning</code> or <code>danger</code>.</li>
    <li><code>data-presentation</code> accepts <code>banner</code> (default), <code>accent</code> or <code>inline</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of each example. <code>onDismiss</code> is optional: without it, the close button is not drawn.</p>
</Base>
